Bus factor is **1**. Andrew Gallant wrote 2,554 of the 4,205 lines still in `src/` (60.7%), which is more than half.

I used `git blame -w -M -C` on HEAD, so whitespace-only and moved lines don't count. That includes the "Fix line endings in error.rs" commit. I merged authors by name only; there is no `.mailmap`.

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Andrew Gallant | 2554 | 60.7% |
| Niko Alvarez | 883 | 21.0% |
| Ola Berg (+ `ola.berg`) | 113 | 2.7% |
| Sebastian Thiel | 74 | 1.8% |
| Ashley | 68 | 1.6% |
| Aron Griffis | 59 | 1.4% |
| Niv Kaminer (+ `nivkner`) | 45 | 1.1% |
| 30 other authors | ~409 | ~9.7% |

- **Generated file:** All 883 of Niko Alvarez's lines are `src/errno_table.rs`, from the commit "Add generated errno table". If you exclude that file, Andrew's share is 76.9% (2554 of 3322), and nobody else has more than 3.4%. Reaching 80% takes two authors (Andrew and Ola Berg) either way.
- **Per-file concentration:** Andrew's share of each file:

  | File | Andrew's share |
  |---|---|
  | `src/tests/util.rs` | 100% |
  | `src/tests/mod.rs` | 100% |
  | `src/tests/recursive.rs` | 87.7% |
  | `src/dent.rs` | 82.7% |
  | `src/lib.rs` | 65.8% |
  | `src/error.rs` | 64.5% |

  `src/util.rs` is the exception. It has only about 100 lines, and Ola Berg owns the majority of them.
- **Alias merges:** I merged "Ola Berg" with "ola.berg", and "Niv Kaminer" with "nivkner". "Alisha" and "Alisha Aneja" are probably one person (9 lines combined), but I left them separate. "Ashley" and "Ashley Mannix" may be one person too, and I left them separate. None of these merges changes the result.

